# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Angel0x1 web — environment template.  COPY to `.env` (gitignored) for local dev,
# and set the SAME keys in your host's dashboard (Vercel → Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables) for production.  NEVER put real secrets in this file, in
# client code, or anywhere under src/ that ships to the browser.
#
# The waitlist endpoint reads these ONLY on the server (src/pages/api/waitlist.ts).
# Until a store is configured the endpoint validates + accepts the email and logs a
# notice; wiring a real store is a drop-in (see README "Wiring real storage").
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Which storage adapter the /api/waitlist function uses: "none" | "supabase"
WAITLIST_STORE="none"

# --- Supabase (only if WAITLIST_STORE="supabase") ---------------------------------
# Use the SERVICE ROLE key (server-only!).  It must live in the host env, never the
# client.  A table `waitlist(email text primary key, created_at timestamptz default now())`.
SUPABASE_URL=""
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""

# Cap for the "free lifetime" cohort shown/computed server-side.
WAITLIST_LIFETIME_CAP="5000"
